[ti:Vox Fantasma (Ghost Tongue)]
[ar:Johnathan "Qasparr" Monroe]
[al:Qasparr the Unfriendly Ghost]
[by:Qasparr karaoke draft — timings estimated]

[00:00.50]Welcome to the séance. Two dead tongues enter — one ghost remains.
[00:03.25]In this corner: the language of EMPIRE... LATIN!
[00:06.00]In this corner: the language of PHILOSOPHERS... GREEK!
[00:08.75]And the ghost? The ghost speaks BOTH. No mercy. No limits.
[00:12.00]Vox fantasma — hear the ghost speak,
[00:15.38]Dead tongues on a living beat,
[00:18.75]Greek to the gutter, Latin to the street,
[00:22.12]Phantasma rising when the languages meet.
[00:26.00]Veni, vidi, vici — I came, I saw, I seized it,
[00:26.84]Latin in my lungs and the empire never eased it.
[00:27.69]Memento mori — remember you must die,
[00:28.53]So every single verse is a headstone for a lie.
[00:29.38]Amor fati — I love the fate they gave me,
[00:30.22]Turned the gutter into gospel, now the struggle never slaved me.
[00:31.06]Ex nihilo — from nothing I was made,
[00:31.91]Built a throne from the gutter, now the ghosts get paid.
[00:32.75]Vox populi — the voice of every people,
[00:33.59]Spit it from the block to the top of the steeple.
[00:34.44]Ad astra — to the stars through the hardship,
[00:35.28]Carved my name in the dark with a masterful penmanship.
[00:36.12]In tenebris — in darkness I was dwelling,
[00:36.97]But the dark taught me the language that the light was never telling.
[00:37.81]Carpe noctem — I seize the night, I own it,
[00:38.66]Every dead tongue living when the ghost is what intones it.
[00:39.50]They called my speech strange, called the dialect a barrier,
[00:40.34]Now the dead tongues live and the living ones are wearier.
[00:41.19]Conjugating conquest while they conjugated doubt,
[00:42.03]Every declension's a lesson that I'm never tapping out.
[00:42.88]Ablative absolute — the city having fallen,
[00:43.72]I rose from the ruins with the ancient tongues a-calling.
[00:44.56]Cogito ergo sum — I think, therefore I haunt,
[00:45.41]Every thought's a phantom and the phantom's what they want.
[00:46.25]Sic semper tyrannis — thus always to the tyrants,
[00:47.09]Broke the chains of empire with the bars of my defiance.
[00:47.94]Vae victis — woe to the conquered, that's their cry,
[00:48.78]But the ghost can't be conquered 'cause the ghost will never die.
[00:49.62]Pax romana? No — I bring the war of words,
[00:50.47]Every syllable a soldier, every metaphor a sword.
[00:51.31]Finis coronat opus — the end crowns the work,
[00:52.16]Dead tongues, living ghost, and the reaper goes berserk.
[00:53.50]Vox fantasma — hear the ghost speak,
[00:56.62]Dead tongues on a living beat,
[00:59.75]Greek to the gutter, Latin to the street,
[01:02.88]Phantasma rising when the languages meet.
[01:06.50]Logos — the Word, and the Word was the weapon,
[01:07.46]Pathos in my pain and the ethos in my stepping.
[01:08.43]Kairos — the moment, and the moment is now,
[01:09.39]Seized it by the throat and I never take a bow.
[01:10.36]Thanatos — death himself couldn't hold me,
[01:11.32]Shadow-boxed the reaper and the reaper never told me.
[01:12.29]Phōnē — the voice, and the voice is a ghost,
[01:13.25]Every frequency haunting from Brightmoor to the coast.
[01:14.21]Psychē — the soul, and the soul never dies,
[01:15.18]Breath of the divine in a gutter full of lies.
[01:16.14]Skia — the shadow, and the shadow's my twin,
[01:17.11]Every light needs a darkness for the vision to begin.
[01:18.07]Nekros — the dead, but the dead never rest,
[01:19.04]When the ghost got a message and the message is the best.
[01:20.00]Hubris — the pride that comes before the fall,
[01:20.96]But the ghost already fell and climbed the highest wall.
[01:21.93]Phantasma in my mouth and it's more than what it seems —
[01:22.89]A ghost, a phantom, and the ghost inside my dreams,
[01:23.86]The fantasy they laughed at when I plotted and I schemed,
[01:24.82]The phantom pain of streets I lost — five meanings in between.
[01:25.79]Eureka — I found it, the cipher's complete,
[01:26.75]Dead languages living on a Brightmoor beat.
[01:27.71]Aletheia — the truth that can't be hidden,
[01:28.68]Every bar's a revelation and the ghost is what was written.
[01:29.64]Telos — the purpose, and the purpose is clear,
[01:30.61]Speak the tongues of ancients 'til the whole world hears.
[01:31.57]Thanatos met phantasma and death had to retreat,
[01:32.54]'Cause you can't kill a ghost that the languages keep.
[01:34.00]Vox fantasma — hear the ghost speak,
[01:37.00]Dead tongues on a living beat,
[01:40.00]Greek to the gutter, Latin to the street,
[01:43.00]Phantasma rising when the languages meet.
[01:46.50]The languages merge and the ghost becomes the teacher,
[01:48.00]Latin in the left hand, Greek in the right — I'm a creature
[01:49.50]Of both worlds, and neither world can claim me,
[01:51.00]Dead tongues gave me life and the living never tamed me.
[01:52.50]Now YOU speak — veni, vidi, vici, say it with your chest,
[01:54.00]Logos in your mouth and let the truth do the rest.
[01:55.50]Memento mori — yeah, remember you must die,
[01:57.00]So speak like every sentence is your last one in the sky.
[01:58.50]Amor fati, kairos — love your moment, seize your time,
[02:00.00]Thanatos is coming but the ghost will never die.
[02:01.50]Phantasma, fantasma — the word itself's the spell,
[02:03.00]Every language is a heaven and a hell.
[02:04.50]I conjugated empires and I declined the fall,
[02:06.00]The ghost speaks every tongue and the ghost outlives them all.
[02:07.50]Ex nihilo to ad astra — from nothing to the stars,
[02:09.00]The gutter was the launchpad and the heavens are ours.
[02:10.50]Finis — but the end is a beginning in disguise,
[02:12.00]Dead tongues, living ghost, and the legend never dies.
[02:27.00]The dust has settled... the smoke has cleared... and the winner is... the GHOST.
[02:28.12]Vox fantasma. Out.
[02:29.25](1) ghost/apparition (literal Greek); (2) phantom (its English child); (3) Qasparr himself —
[02:30.38]the Unfriendly Ghost; (4) fantasy — what they called his dreams when they laughed; (5) phantom
[02:31.50]pain — the streets he lost still ache. Phonetic chains: phantasma/fantasma/miasma/plasma;
[02:32.62]mori/glory/story; fati/vati (prophet). Flow note: Latin verse staccato and percussive
[02:33.75](imperial cadence), Greek verse smoother and rolling — the contrast IS the performance.*
[02:34.88]---
